              "I recommend **updating the existing overview and creating an r3 revision of the plan within the same investigation**.\n\nThe scientific model and broad objective remain unchanged. The strategy now has a more specific target. The overview should remain the stable entry point, while a new plan revision makes sense because r2 is largely organized around the completed B02/E03 work.\n\nFor the **overview**, I would consolidate its current sections around:\n\n- What is established: the conditional realization, high-count oscillation, and complete count-tail bounds.\n- The central unresolved question: whether the complete theta source supplies an independent signed relation between neighboring count sectors.\n- The primary candidate: the Gaussian collision test, initially for double events.\n- The secondary option: Green-potential acquisition, conditional on demonstrating a useful comparison with direct source evaluation.\n\nThe new connections should retain their proof-author status; the strategy is promising, not an established collision mechanism.\n\nFor **plan r3**, I would specify a bounded sequence:\n\n1. Verify the exact count dictionary and error transfer being consumed.\n2. Seek one source-specific signed estimate on a declared time/window/scale, with the collision controls and scalar comparison included.\n3. Issue E09/E10 only when there is a concrete lemma and useful consequence—or record the precise missing premise and stop that attempted approach.\n\nHigher multiplicities would remain a stated extension. OA’s deflation methods would be supporting tools; Green acquisition would remain the fallback.\n\nKeep r2 as historical, retain the existing sole progress register, and update the README and continuation links together when adopting r3.\n\nI recorded this recommendation in §8 of the [brainstorm note](/Users/ebbaker/Documents/shifted-zeta-positivity/papers/investigations-5/08_theta_observables_newman_dynamics/01_direct_newman_realization/brainstorm/notes/03_TND_D_CROSS_BRANCH_RESEARCH_BRAINSTORM_20261109.md)."
            ]
          },
